{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Lost and Found in Tokyo**\n\nStepping off the plane in Tokyo, the first thing that hits you is the energy. It's a electric hum, a blend of neon lights and ancient tradition that feels entirely unique to this city. My journey began in Shinjuku, where skyscrapers pierce the clouds and the streets below are a river of people moving with purpose.\n\nThe contrast is what makes Japan so magical. One moment, you are navigating the chaos of a bustling train station, and the next, you are sitting in a quiet temple garden in Asakusa, listening to the soft rustle of bamboo. I spent a delightful afternoon wandering through Senso-ji Temple, the air thick with the scent of incense. The vibrant red pagoda stood as a silent guardian against the backdrop of modern billboards.\n\nFood is an adventure in itself. From slurping steaming bowls of ramen in tiny alleyway shops to enjoying the precision of a multi-course kaiseki dinner, every bite told a story. The convenience stores, often overlooked by travelers, offered surprisingly delicious bento boxes and fresh fruit that became my daily fuel.\n\nAs the sun set, the city transformed. The streets in Shibuya glowed with an almost surreal brightness. Crossing the famous scramble intersection, surrounded by thousands of strangers yet feeling completely connected, was a highlight I'll never forget.\n\nJapan is a place where the future and the past dance together seamlessly. It challenges you to look closer, slow down, and appreciate the details. Whether you are seeking spiritual peace or urban excitement, this country delivers an experience that lingers long after you return home. I'm already planning my next trip.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Lost", "logprob": -3.6152272}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.2362727}, {"token": " Found", "logprob": -2.384186e-07}, {"token": " in", "logprob": 